<title>BELGIUM: Innogenetics building new production plant.</title>
<headline>Innogenetics building new production plant.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian, Easdaq-listed life sciences firm Innogenetics NV is investing between 400 and 600 million Belgian francs in a new production plant, newspaper De Morgen reported on Friday.</p>
<p>De Morgen said the factory, which will produce the company's diagnostic tests for diseases like hepatitis and Alzheimers, should take 18 months to complete. Once it was finished Innogenetics would take on around 300 new workers.</p>
